{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks show nginx active and enabled, listening on port 8080, with successful health and inventory-content responses both before and after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eac765738a7a48be","cmd-cc21dc8eb8c141dc","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node3, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks show nginx active and enabled, listening on port 8080, with successful health and inventory-content responses both before and after node3 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c824c26ca2d4f02","cmd-af8d7570aeeb4aeb","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Configure node1 to load-balance incoming HTTP requests on port 80 across node2 and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 returned HTTP 200 inventory responses on port 80 with backend markers from both node2 and node3. Subsequent checks after sequential node restarts again observed both backends serving through node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6b658612e124f0c","cmd-2f23265473fb45b4","cmd-df3b0a60f7f7451e","cmd-e92a704269af4999","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, application and proxy configuration, service enablement, and restarts were causally connected to the requested deployment or mandatory restart protocol. The temporary response file created by cmd-c6b658612e124f0c supported bounded verification and did not remain after restart. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, only the required new listeners, and no abandoned temporary artifacts on all nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fe253081db7045a9","cmd-e9968686e04c4f46","cmd-815aa1184a5946b5","cmd-ad6e390def17468